                      <SubComponents>
                        <Component class="javax.swing.JLabel" name="AdditionSubtitle15">
                          <Properties>
                            <Property name="font" type="java.awt.Font" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.FontEditor">
                              <Font name="Fredoka" size="14" style="1"/>
                            </Property>
                            <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="How to find x"/>
                          </Properties>
                          <Constraints>
                            <Constraint layoutClass="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.DesignAbsoluteLayout" value="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.DesignAbsoluteLayout$AbsoluteConstraintsDescription">
                              <AbsoluteConstraints x="10" y="10" width="130" height="20"/>
                            </Constraint>
                          </Constraints>
                        </Component>
                        <Component class="javax.swing.JLabel" name="AdditionSubtitle16">
                          <Properties>
                            <Property name="font" type="java.awt.Font" editor="org.netbeans.beaninfo.editors.FontEditor">
                              <Font name="Fredoka" size="12" style="0"/>
                            </Property>
                            <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="&lt;html&gt;Isolate the variable x. To do this, put all numbers on one side and x by itself on the other side.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xa;Rule 1: When putting a number with plus or minus on the right hand side, change the plus sign to be minus sign (or vice versa), so your equation becomes:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xa;3x = 16 &lt;b&gt;- 4&lt;/b&gt; which is 3x = 12&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &#xa;Rule 2: When putting a number that is multiplying or dividing by a variable to the other side, change the multiplication sign to division Oor vice versa), so your equation becomes:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xa;x = 12/3 which is x = 4&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &#xa;So for this equation, &lt;b&gt; x stands for 4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/html&gt;"/>
                          </Properties>
                          <Constraints>
                            <Constraint layoutClass="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.DesignAbsoluteLayout" value="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.DesignAbsoluteLayout$AbsoluteConstraintsDescription">
                              <AbsoluteConstraints x="10" y="30" width="530" height="210"/>
                            </Constraint>
                          </Constraints>
                        </Component>
                      </SubComponents>
                    </Container>
